{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Quick-start"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Creating a cross-platform SwiftCrossUI app with Swift Bundler."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This quick start guide uses "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler"},{"type":"text","text":". Although not strictly required, it simplifies many aspects of cross-platform distribution and provides a platform-agnostic configuration format for specifying things such as app icons and custom URL schemes."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’re new to Swift, we recommend starting with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/Setting-up-a-development-environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Installing-Swift-Bundler","text":"Installing Swift Bundler"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Follow "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/stackotter\/swift-bundler?tab=readme-ov-file#installation-"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mint"},{"type":"text","text":" is the preferred installation method on macOS and Linux as of the last update to this quick start guide."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Installing-system-dependencies","text":"Installing system dependencies"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Each backend has different requirements. In this guide we’ll use ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/DefaultBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" which uses ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on macOS, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/GtkBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on Linux, ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/WinUIBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on Windows, and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" on iOS\/tvOS. Click through the backend relevant to your machine for detailed installation requirements. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/AppKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftCrossUI\/documentation\/SwiftCrossUI\/UIKitBackend","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" have no system dependencies.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Using-Swift-Bundlers-SwiftCrossUI-template","text":"Using Swift Bundler’s SwiftCrossUI template"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swift Bundler provides many built-in templates; we’ll use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftCrossUI"},{"type":"text","text":" template uses "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DefaultBackend"},{"type":"text","text":" to select the most appropriate backend at compile time."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["swift bundler create HelloWorld --template SwiftCrossUI","cd HelloWorld"],"syntax":"sh"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Running-your-app","text":"Running your app"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Running your new app with Swift Bundler is as simple as it gets!"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":